WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.901
Mandy could not believe it.

2
00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:05.837
She was aboard the Santa Maria

3
00:00:05.838 --> 00:00:09.170
. And it was sailing away from the

4
00:00:09.171 --> 00:00:12.932
dock. "Where is Vinnie?" she

5
00:00:12.933 --> 00:00:15.868
wondered. Diego had disappeared

6
00:00:15.869 --> 00:00:19.368
too. Then Mandy spotted a familiar

7
00:00:19.369 --> 00:00:24.495
figure. It was Christopher Columbus, and he was speaking with some

8
00:00:24.496 --> 00:00:28.630
sailors. "Excuse me, sir!" she called

9
00:00:28.631 --> 00:00:32.189
out. Mandy took the book out of her

10
00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:35.330
pocket. A sailor grabbed her

11
00:00:35.331 --> 00:00:39.987
arm. "How did you get on the ship?" he asked,

12
00:00:39.988 --> 00:00:42.818
surprised. "You’re a little

13
00:00:42.819 --> 00:00:47.062
girl!" "Wait a minute!" Christopher Columbus

14
00:00:47.063 --> 00:00:50.504
interrupted. "What do you have in your

15
00:00:50.505 --> 00:00:55.198
hand?" "This is why I’m here, sir," explained

16
00:00:55.199 --> 00:00:58.052
Mandy. "I found your book in the

17
00:00:58.053 --> 00:01:01.427
church. I knew it was important to

18
00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:05.396
you." "I thought it was lost," Columbus

19
00:01:05.397 --> 00:01:08.303
said. "This must be a sign from

20
00:01:08.304 --> 00:01:11.388
God. You have brought good luck for our

21
00:01:11.389 --> 00:01:16.555
journey." On another part of the ship, Vinnie was looking

22
00:01:16.556 --> 00:01:23.332
around. After he helped gather the spilled potatoes, Vinnie had somehow lost

23
00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:26.440
Mandy. The ship was full of

24
00:01:26.441 --> 00:01:30.525
activity. The Santa Maria was long and

25
00:01:30.526 --> 00:01:34.894
narrow. Vinnie counted more than 35 sailors

26
00:01:34.895 --> 00:01:41.652
aboard. They were uncoiling ropes, connecting equipment, and opening the large, white

27
00:01:41.653 --> 00:01:46.314
sails. Before he knew it, the ship was in open

28
00:01:46.315 --> 00:01:50.360
water. "I wonder what Mandy’s doing," he

29
00:01:50.361 --> 00:01:52.898
thought. He looked behind

30
00:01:52.899 --> 00:01:56.975
him. The Niña and Pinta were following

31
00:01:56.976 --> 00:02:01.127
closely. They were smaller ships with fewer

32
00:02:01.128 --> 00:02:05.818
sailors. "Don’t just stand there," said a young boy about Vinnie’s age.

33
00:02:05.819 --> 00:02:08.506
He was holding a mop.

34
00:02:08.507 --> 00:02:12.732
"You’ll get in trouble. Here, take this."

35
00:02:12.733 --> 00:02:16.417
"But, I’m not—," Vinnie began.

36
00:02:16.418 --> 00:02:19.567
The boy gave Vinnie an odd look.

37
00:02:19.568 --> 00:02:23.122
A big sailor walked over to them.

38
00:02:23.123 --> 00:02:27.368
"Why are you just standing there?" he demanded.

39
00:02:27.369 --> 00:02:29.885
"Get to work!"

40
00:02:29.886 --> 00:02:32.643
"Yes, sir!" cried Vinnie.

41
00:02:32.644 --> 00:02:36.027
He started mopping the deck quickly.

42
00:02:36.028 --> 00:02:38.642
The sailor walked away.

43
00:02:38.643 --> 00:02:42.984
"Thanks for the warning," Vinnie said to the boy.

44
00:02:42.985 --> 00:02:46.294
"I’m Manuel," the boy said.

45
00:02:46.295 --> 00:02:48.798
"This is my first time sailing.

46
00:02:48.799 --> 00:02:50.579
How about you?"

47
00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:54.151
"My first time too," said Vinnie.

48
00:02:54.152 --> 00:02:57.719
Together, the boys mopped the deck.

49
00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:01.387
It was wet from the mist of the ocean waves.

50
00:03:01.388 --> 00:03:08.356
Meanwhile, Mandy stood listening as Christopher Columbus spoke to some of his crew.

51
00:03:08.357 --> 00:03:13.218
She realized that each of them had a different job.

52
00:03:13.219 --> 00:03:15.933
One man was a carpenter.

53
00:03:15.934 --> 00:03:18.498
Another was a cook.

54
00:03:18.499 --> 00:03:22.915
A silversmith and a doctor were on board too.

55
00:03:22.916 --> 00:03:27.558
"Unexpected things happen at sea," Columbus was saying.

56
00:03:27.559 --> 00:03:32.232
"Each of you has a duty to make sure this voyage is successful."

57
00:03:32.233 --> 00:03:38.618
"Any wood that needs repair, the men can see me," said the carpenter.

58
00:03:38.619 --> 00:03:43.471
"I’ll keep the meat well salted," said the cook.

59
00:03:43.472 --> 00:03:50.140
"Captain, I’ll make sure your instruments are working perfectly," said the silversmith.

60
00:03:50.141 --> 00:03:57.180
"If any men get sick or break their bones, I will take care of them," said the doctor.

61
00:03:57.181 --> 00:04:03.704
"Good. And every day, I expect a report from each of you," said Columbus.

62
00:04:03.705 --> 00:04:14.705
"Yes, Captain," the men said.

